# This node_modules ships as part of stories-engine itself (extraResource,
# see quasar.config.js + shellAssembly.js's own comment) and gets
# relocated by ordinary means after packaging — a real installer, a zip
# extract, a plain drag-and-drop move to wherever the user installs the
# app. pnpm's default (isolated, symlink-heavy .pnpm store) is NOT reliably
# relocatable that way: confirmed by an actual test (moving this folder
# broke module resolution — "Cannot find module ...quasar.js" — right
# after a working in-place test). hoisted = one flat node_modules, no
# internal symlinks to survive a move (confirmed by a second real test:
# moved + ran `quasar dev` successfully from the new location), at the
# cost of some duplicated nested deps — worth it, this is the ONLY
# node_modules in the project ever shipped as data rather than run in
# place.
#
# NOTE: this file alone was NOT reliably picked up in testing here (`pnpm
# config get node-linker` kept reporting undefined even with this file
# present and correctly formatted — root cause not pinned down, possibly
# the nested pnpm-workspace.yaml at the repo root confusing pnpm's
# workspace-root detection). Kept for whichever environment DOES honor it,
# but package.json's `vendor:game-shell` script passes
# `--config.node-linker=hoisted` explicitly on the command line too — that
# one is confirmed to always take effect regardless, treat it as the real
# mechanism this depends on.
node-linker=hoisted
